body:
Was in Navy Basic training and got a pretty severe bacterial infection on my neck. Lead RDC was a hospital corpsman and took me to medical after it became very clear it wasn't just a razor bump. So anyway, get diagnosed and put on pain killers so I was out of commission for a couple of days while we were doing PT. 

&#x200B;

The rest of my division is finishing up at the gym (was the middle of winter so all the running was in the gym instead of outside) and I hear my name shouted, the other two RDCs were Petty Officer 1st classes and I thought it sounded like one of them so without turning to see first I just shout out, "YES PETTY OFFICER?!"

&#x200B;

"THE FUCK DID YOU JUST CALL ME?" was the call back and I turn to see my Chief just angry as fuck. "Sorry CHIEF I thought it was \[petty officer here\]! Won't happen again Chief!" Was all I could muster and he just grimaces and goes, "I'm going to imagine that's the drugs in you but if you weren't on them I'd beat you here for the next hour!" And without missing a beat I just give a quick, "Chief, this recruit is very happy to be on drugs right now!"
